# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build context for the triage image. Owner: Yeo Kai Yuan (Part 1).
#
# The image needs exactly two things: requirements.txt and service/. Everything
# listed here is excluded so that:
#   * the 45 MB course CSV and our 1,000 team rows never enter an image — the
#     service must only ever see tickets that arrive through POST /tickets;
#   * results, logs and .jtl files stay out, so an image can never be confused
#     with evidence;
#   * the build context stays small, which keeps `docker compose build` quick.
#
# Excludes are listed explicitly rather than with a `*` + `!service` allow-list,
# because an explicit list is what a reader can check against `ls`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Version control and local tooling
.git
.gitignore
.venv
venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov

# Datasets — never in an image
ict3113_tickets.csv
data
golden
labelling

# Evidence and outputs
results
logs
analysis
predictions
workload
models
slides

# Host-side tooling, docs and tests
tests
scripts
jmeter
docs
requirements-dev.txt
pyproject.toml
README.md
*.md
*.docx

# Container definitions themselves (not needed inside the image)
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml

# Local secrets and scratch. .env is gitignored; it must not be baked in either —
# configuration is passed at run time by docker-compose.yml.
.env
.env.example
*.tmp
*.bak
scratch
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
